    <node id="&quot;LPUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LPUs, or language processing units, are the core technology of Groq that enable high-performance inference-as-a-service offerings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SRAM, or static random access memory, is a type of memory used in Groq's LPUs, noted for its speed compared to high-bandwidth memory (HBM)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HBM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HBM, or high-bandwidth memory, is a type of memory used in GPUs, which Groq's LPUs are compared against for performance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LLAMA 3.3 70B&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Llama 3.3 70B is a benchmark model that Groq's chips can process at a rate of 350 tokens per second."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GPT-OSS 120B&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"gpt-oss 120B is another benchmark model that Groq's chips can process at a rate of 465 tokens per second."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1 TB/S&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1 TB/s is the memory bandwidth achieved by a single HBM3e stack, providing context for the performance comparison with Groq's LPUs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;8 TB/S&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"8 TB/s is the total memory bandwidth per GPU achieved with HBM, highlighting the performance capabilities of Nvidia's GPUs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;10 TO 80 TIMES FASTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"10 to 80 times faster indicates the performance advantage of Groq's SRAM over HBM, emphasizing its potential in high-performance applications."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;574 LPUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"574 LPUs are required to run Llama 70B, illustrating the scale of resources needed for high-performance inference."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;23 KILOWATTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"23 kilowatts is the power consumption of Cerebras' WSE-3 wafers, indicating the energy demands of high-performance chips."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARTIFICIAL ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Artificial Analysis is the benchmarking entity that reported Groq's chips can churn out 350 tokens per second for Llama 3.3 70B."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VON NEUMANN ARCHITECTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Von Neumann architecture is a traditional computing architecture that Groq's assembly line architecture aims to improve upon."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DATA FLOW ARCHITECTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Data flow architecture is a programmable design used in Groq's chips to accelerate linear algebra calculations during inference."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASSEMBLY LINE ARCHITECTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Assembly line architecture is a unique design by Groq intended to enhance the processing of data in its chips."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-BANDWIDTH MEMORY (HBM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-bandwidth memory (HBM) is a type of memory used in GPUs, which Groq's LPUs are compared against for performance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEMORY BANDWIDTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Memory bandwidth refers to the rate at which data can be read from or written to memory, a critical factor in chip performance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFERENCE-AS-A-SERVICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inference-as-a-service is a service model that Groq offers, allowing users to leverage its high-performance LPUs for AI tasks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLOBAL MEMORY SHORTAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Global memory shortage refers to the current demand and supply imbalance for memory technologies, impacting the industry."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e470dedd05b45c97fe6e4fc7e8acb60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTITRUST LAWSUIT&quot;">
